# Named exceptions to bootstrap-check's placeholder check ([C1], [C3] in scripts/bootstrap-check.sh).
# One entry per line: `<path>: <text> -- <reason>`. An entry exempts that exact text in that file only.
# An entry without a reason, for a file the check does not read, or matching nothing any more fails
# the check (conformance/test-placeholder-allow.py proves each of those), so the list cannot go stale.
# An entry hides EVERY occurrence of its text in its file: name notation only -- an append-only
# record that quotes `box-<checkout>-<model>` and may not be reworded -- never a template's own
# field names, which are the unfilled fields this check exists to find.
#
# Ships empty. A project adds an entry when a record it may not edit carries placeholder-shaped text.
